                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 29 at 1:25AM MST until October 30 at 10:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall over saturated\nsoils and waterways that flooded as recently as last week.\n\n* WHERE...Yavapai County and northern Gila County.\n\n* WHEN...From 10 AM MST Friday morning through 10 PM MST Friday\nevening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flash flooding will be possible in creeks, normally dry\nwashes, swimming holes, and over recently burned areas. Low-water\ncrossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Another round of tropical moisture arrives in central Arizona\nFriday morning. Expect generalized accumulations of 0.50\" to\n1.00\" of rainfall within the watch area, locally higher amounts\nof up to 2.00\" possible in thunderstorms.\n- Additional information is available at weather.gov/flagstaff.",
                "instruction": "Have a way to receive Flash Flood Warnings and be prepared to take\naction should warnings be issued.",
