                "senderName": "NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 29 at 1:05AM MST until October 30 at 10:00PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of south central Arizona, including the following\nareas, Dripping Springs, Globe/Miami, Mazatzal Mountains,\nPinal/Superstition Mountains, San Carlos, Southeast Gila County,\nSuperior and Tonto Basin.\n\n* WHEN...From Friday afternoon through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nLow-water crossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Abundant moisture over the area will combine with an incoming\nweather system to provide for showers and thunderstorms on\nFriday, some of which are expected to produce moderate to heavy\nrainfall. Any strong thunderstorms will have the potential to\nproduce rainfall rates as high as 1-2 inches per hour. Localized\nrainfall amounts of one to two inches are expected within the\nWatch area on Friday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
